# Personal Blog Change-Log

## Background

  This site will operate as a personal blog and a place to build and test web applications I build.
  This file will act as a change log for a more detailed understanding of changes made over time.
  The updates will reflect pushes to Github and will be used to track the evolution of the project.
  Each entry will include a brief description of the changes made, along with the date and author of the change.

## Rules:
  1. Each entry should be concise and clearly describe the change made.
  2. Entries should be listed in reverse chronological order, with the most recent changes at the top
  3. Each entry should include the date of the change, the author, and a brief description
  4. Avoid using technical jargon or overly complex language; the goal is to make the change log accessible to all team members and stakeholders.
  5. Before pushing changes to the repository, ensure that the change log is updated with the latest modifications.

